Yes. After looking across the current open-source landscape, I would **not merely “improve the Postiz analytics page.”** I would turn the fork into a **Media OS / Mission Control** whose distribution engine happens to be Postiz.

The strongest projects I found each contain a piece of what we want:

* Postiz — distribution/scheduling/integrations.
* BrightBean Studio — arguably the best open-source reference for analytics + inbox + agent-accessible social operations.
* TryPost — brand profiles + MCP + agent-first social control.
* Social Stats — analytics/AI insights/unified inbox ideas.
* Mission Control — the best reference for the actual **agent fleet control-plane**.
* Tutti — exceptional inspiration for individual-agent live inspection.
* Langfuse — traces/evals/prompts/cost/experiments.
* LangGraph — durable, resumable, human-gated agent workflows.

The result should look less like Buffer and more like **Bloomberg Terminal + factory control room for an autonomous media company**.

