# Agent governance

Mission Control's quality gates are particularly worth copying. It explicitly supports review stages before tasks are considered complete. ([GitHub][5])

Every agent task should have:

```text
INPUT CONTRACT
OUTPUT CONTRACT
EVALUATOR
RETRY POLICY
MAX COST
TIMEOUT
APPROVAL REQUIREMENT
```

Example:

```yaml
agent: script_writer

input:
  research_packet: required

output:
  script.json: required

gate:
  factuality_score: ">=0.95"
  unsupported_claims: 0

budget:
  max_usd: 0.10

retry:
  max_attempts: 3

publish_permission: false
```

Agent permissions matter.

Research Agent:

```text
READ web
READ knowledge
WRITE research
```

Publisher:

```text
READ approved content
WRITE social platforms
```

Strategist:

```text
READ analytics
WRITE recommendations
NO publishing
```

No agent should automatically inherit every tool.

